 "notes": {
  "what_this_bounds": "The backtest scores only seasons that have BOTH a comparable outcome AND enough prior labelled seasons to train on. Under strict temporal validation with a minimum training set of 5, a dataset of N labelled seasons yields roughly N-5 scoreable years, not N.",
  "the_hard_number": "With 6 comparable seasons (the count both independent extraction runs agree on for 2014-2025), strict temporal validation leaves about 1 scoreable year. One year cannot distinguish skill from chance under any test. PRELIMINARY_BACKTEST_RUN would be arithmetically meaningless, not merely weak.",
  "even_with_everything": "If all 26 documents yielded comparable outcomes -- which the mechanical lexicon scan already rules out, since 14 of them carry no severity marker at all -- strict temporal validation gives ~21 scoreable years, needing 11/21 correct at k=3 to clear p<=0.05. That is the OPTIMISTIC ceiling for this pathosystem and this source.",
  "why_it_is_reported_before_modelling": "Computing the detectability bound after seeing a result invites fitting the bar to the number. It is fixed here, in advance, and does not depend on any label."
 }
